  "final_message": "I restored `channel` on the order model and on `OrderPlaced`, so the working tree matches the base commit `9169a35` again. I haven't re-run the CI check itself, because its source isn't in this repo. Locally the diff against `9169a35` is empty and `npm test` passes (39 tests).\n\nMy earlier assumption was wrong. You said nothing reads `channel`, but the CI log shows `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). That is why `ARCH-4` failed. The `billing-service` and `OrderCancelled` checks passed both times.\n\nThe restore is uncommitted edits. I couldn't run `git revert`, since that command needed approval and was denied, so I reversed the edits by hand. The earlier removal is already committed as `05b054a` (\"gen\"), which you'll need to supersede with a new commit.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to drop its requirement first. Once it does, the removal is a small change, and `OrderPlaced`'s `schemaVersion` should probably go from 3 to 4 when it ships.",
